After a wrong answer, discard the candidate's whole rule, not merely its selected color or endpoint. Explicitly contrast its test prediction with all complete demonstrations, including unchanged lookalike cases, and change course only for an interpretation supported by that evidence. A depleted demo budget is not evidence that the remaining guess is correct. Keep output actions grounded in full demo replay rather than using repeated near-duplicate submissions to probe the grader.

In long demonstration streams, repeated skill/reference loading is not analysis: load applicable guidance once, process each newly returned pair against earlier ones, then choose one action. In protocol-constrained ARC, the response should be exactly one action JSON object.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545321/attempts/695f0949c61e4d9285c5659d167e433e/system/state/hermes/skills/arc/arc-demo-synthesis/references/rejected-submissions-and-review.md"}
